Save93 equipment comparison of the Papyrus Tweaks exclusion list, 2026-11-10 14:24 build / AE 1.6.1170 / SSE Display Tweaks limiter 42 FPS (three launches) and 30 FPS (one launch), DynamicUpdateBudget=false / Papyrus bEnableLogging=0, bEnableProfiling=1
APB_GAMEPLAY_TRACE=catchup-exclusions, APB_CATCHUP_MODE=accelerate, APB_CATCHUP_TARGET=60, EngageBelowFPS 50, direct judgement on.
Catch-up is ON in every trial. "on" = exclusion list used (release behaviour). "off" = list left out through the test control VMCatchUp::SetExclusionList(false): the classes UI, ConsoleUtil, PO3_SKSEFunctions, MfgConsole, MFGConsoleFunc, Input, Debug, Utility, PapyrusTweaks, Quest and the prefixes GetAnimation, GetQuest are then judged by the name rule alone. The known-change list (WornObject.GetDisplayName, NiOverride.GetItemUniqueID/GetObjectUniqueID) applies in both.
Test DLL APBGameplayTrace.dll sha256 8dbde4f630203d3f504a6b3b9d35a21a6913df8085adc4743d59fc83268ecc86 (release DLL of the same source: 1385930f...; the release plugin never calls the test control).
Order off,on,on,off,on,off,off,on per launch (build/catchup/run-effect-ab.ps1 -TraceMode catchup-exclusions). Compare trials with the same handler count.
The game window was in front for all four launches; foreground_pct was 100.0 in all 32 trials. guard_violations and overrun_pauses were 0 in all 32.
Note: at 42 FPS all twelve list-off trials had 174 handlers, so the 202-handler case has no list-off trial at that limit.

